The log files from the header information are attached here.

- Science exposure (UDS_PSG1 for LS_J, S20B095_Mask1 for LS_H)
- Telluric Standard Star data (HIP115119 for LS_J, HIP59174 for LS_H)
- Dome flats (lamp-on and off)
- ThAr arclamp data
- Mask image for ThAr.

The tarball for LS_H also contains some acquisition & count check images.
Sorry about it.

The data was taken in the repeat of the A-B dithers (not ABBA). For
standard sta data, we use one of the available slit(s) on MOS for
standard star observation. We visually check where the continuum is...

You can find the grims information on the LS_J and LS_H from below.
https://www.naoj.org/Instruments/MOIRCS/spec_sensitivity.html

Please be careful about the handling of the data. Though they are
already open to public via SMOKA archive, we don't want the data to be
used beyond our control.
